From fb53aa14b517faed77c7bccffd279c75066726ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 09:39:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] alsa_adapter: don't let snd_mixer_load failure veto
 stream open
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

snd_mixer_load walks every kcontrol on the card, and exotic vendor
controls can refuse reads: the mt6878-mt6369 card (Volla Phone Plinius)
has a BYTES control whose get handler returns EPERM, which failed the
whole load and with it RenderOpenImpl/CaptureOpenImpl — every OHOS
playback session died with 'SndOpenMixer failed' and AVPlayer went to
PLAYER_STATE_ERROR before a single frame.

The adapter never element-accesses through the snd_mixer handle (all
mixer work goes through the snd_ctl name-based API in SndElementWrite/
SndElementRead*), so a failed load only needs a warning: close the
handle and open the stream anyway.

Change-Id: Iaa2ebf60d399d4fe505f664e43728f8fd2e9d82d
Signed-off-by: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
---
 audio/supportlibs/alsa_adapter/src/alsa_soundcard.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/audio/supportlibs/alsa_adapter/src/alsa_soundcard.c b/audio/supportlibs/alsa_adapter/src/alsa_soundcard.c
index 093905613..304569d94 100644
--- a/audio/supportlibs/alsa_adapter/src/alsa_soundcard.c
+++ b/audio/supportlibs/alsa_adapter/src/alsa_soundcard.c
@@ -635,13 +635,19 @@ int32_t SndOpenMixer(struct AlsaSoundCard *cardIns)
 
     ret = snd_mixer_load(cardIns->mixerHandle);
     if (ret < 0) {
-        AUDIO_FUNC_LOGE("Failed to load mixer element: %{public}s.", snd_strerror(ret));
+        /* Non-fatal: loading walks every kcontrol on the card, and exotic
+         * vendor controls can refuse reads (mt6878-mt6369 has a BYTES
+         * control whose get handler returns EPERM), which would otherwise
+         * veto opening the stream. The adapter never element-accesses
+         * through this handle — all mixer work goes through the snd_ctl
+         * name-based API — so drop the handle and carry on. */
+        AUDIO_FUNC_LOGW("mixer element load failed (%{public}s), continuing without mixer handle",
+            snd_strerror(ret));
         ret = snd_mixer_close(cardIns->mixerHandle);
         if (ret < 0) {
             AUDIO_FUNC_LOGE("mixer close error: %{public}s.", snd_strerror(ret));
         }
         cardIns->mixerHandle = NULL;
-        return HDF_FAILURE;
     }
     return HDF_SUCCESS;
 }
